<div class="we-customer-review__header we-customer-review__header--user">
  <span dir="ltr" id="ember10319283" class="we-truncate we-truncate--single-line ember-view we-customer-review__user">  Lillymae Jeune
</span>

  <span class="we-customer-review__separator">, </span>

  <time data-test-customer-review-date datetime="2019-06-06T15:00:21.000Z" aria-label="6 June 2019" class="we-customer-review__date" >06/06/2019</time>
</div>

<h3 dir="ltr" id="we-customer-review-41261" class="we-truncate we-truncate--single-line ember-view we-customer-review__title">  Deleting messages !
</h3>

  <blockquote id="ember10319284" class="we-truncate we-truncate--multi-line we-truncate--interactive ember-view we-customer-review__body">      

      <p dir=false data-test-bidi>so basically the way it works is that the app is kind of like a house. when you open the app its like when you ring the bell or knock on the front door. it lets all your friends know that you’re in the house. so then you can wait for your friends to invite you to their rooms or wave at your friends to ask them to come into a room with you. after you have your friends gathered, you can lock the room so other people don’t come in. so yeah, it’s really fun bc you don’t need to call your friends individually, you can just talk to whoever is available. we have also had “lock wars” where two people fight to keep the room locked or unlocked, and we’ve invaded our friend’s rooms. &gt;😃 but other than that you can just chill with your friends and talk as if you were in a normal call.</p>

  


<!----></blockquote>

<!----></div>
              
</div>
          
    
